  "quotes": [
    {
      "block": "原句1",
      "no": 1,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Logan was playing for Team USA in a contentious gold medal matchup with Team Canada",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 174
        }
      ],
      "words": 15
    },
    {
      "block": "原句2",
      "no": 2,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "\"That's my girl!\"",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1085
        }
      ],
      "words": 3
    },
    {
      "block": "原句3",
      "no": 3,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "And my sister-in-law! cheered Alan, his wedding band glinting from his finger",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1130
        }
      ],
      "words": 12
    },
    {
      "block": "原句4",
      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Over the past year, Levi and I had become friends again, bonding over our love for hockey and Logan",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 1409
        }
      ],
      "words": 19
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I still hadn't talked to my parents, but Logan had encouraged me to reach out to my sister after Meredith had \"liked\" so",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2412
        }
      ],
      "words": 26
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I had money set aside for her to go to college, and I hoped she'd take me up on the offer to pay for her education. To d",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 2759
        }
      ],
      "words": 31
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "The final period was intense. Both teams wanted to win, and neither was giving up any points",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3330
        }
      ],
      "words": 17
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "She'd done it! Logan had done it. I was so proud of her. So happy for her",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3891
        }
      ],
      "words": 17
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "She was one of the most decorated and highly paid female hockey players",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 3965
        }
      ],
      "words": 13
    },
    {
      "block": "原句10",
      "no": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "our work with the NHL culture board had expanded her vision, and she now advocated for women not just as athletes but as",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 4293
        }
      ],
      "words": 27
    },
    {
      "block": "原句11",
      "no": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "We'd definitely pushed some boundaries—on a ski lift, in my room before my roommate returned, in a darkened hallway",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6341
        }
      ],
      "words": 19
    },
    {
      "block": "原句12",
      "no": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Levi and me flanking his sister, our friendship stronger than ever",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 6810
        }
      ],
      "words": 11
    },
    {
      "block": "原句13",
      "no": 13,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "If someone had told me this was how my life would've turned out when I was seventeen, I would've never believed them",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7025
        }
      ],
      "words": 22
    },
    {
      "block": "原句14",
      "no": 14,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "A family where forgiveness was possible and love was unconditional",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 7333
        }
      ],
      "words": 10
    }
  ],
